+For endpoints
+\[
+T_i^0=M_i+N_i+1,\qquad T_i^1=M_i+N_i+2,
+\]
+any single policy whose first \(T\) actions do not depend on the evaluation horizon \(T\) satisfies
+\[
+\max\{R_{T_i^0},R_{T_i^1}\}\ge N_i/4-M_i-O(1).
+\]
+Thus
+\[
+\limsup_T R_T/T\ge 1/4.
